Sound regression checks (run from the workspace root in WSL):

  bash executor/tests/run-sdl-sound-tests.sh
  bash executor/tests/run-mace-tests.sh

The SDL test exercises playback, stop while a callback is waiting, idle silence,
restart and worker shutdown. The MACE test checks reference PCM hashes, stereo
downmix, output bounds and invalid packets. Its xorshift input starts at
0x12345678 and contains 2048 bytes. Golden hashes were generated by FFmpeg 6.1.1
using AIFF-C MAC3/MAC6 fixtures and unsigned 8-bit PCM output, without resampling.
Math Rabbit's intro was also compared byte-for-byte against FFmpeg's output.
No app resources or external decoder programs are needed to run these tests.

MACE decoding is adapted from FFmpeg libavcodec/mace.c at commit
aafb5c655edc76a753275c383ebb139feb032718:
https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/aafb5c655edc76a753275c383ebb139feb032718/libavcodec/mace.c
The decoder retains its LGPL 2.1-or-later notice. The license is distributed in
src/COPYING.LGPLv2.1 and beside the staged executor.exe. The runtime does not
depend on FFmpeg libraries. Note-synth commands currently use square-wave
tones; arbitrary instrument and wave-table synthesis is not implemented.
